From: Gryphfield
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Put the Dock icon on a macOS-style rounded square.

Port of CrossOver 26.3's CW Hack 25964. Windows icons are usually square or
free-form, and look out of place in the Dock next to macOS app icons. The
largest of the program's icons is now drawn into a 512x512 image on Apple's
icon grid (an 824/1024 rounded square with a soft shadow). An icon whose edges
are partly filled is inset so it does not touch the rounded corners; one that
fills its edges, or has nothing on them, is masked whole.

CrossOver loads the rounded-square mask from a PNG in CrossOver.app; here it
is drawn with NSBezierPath, so nothing outside Wine is needed. The edge scan
also uses one byte per pixel instead of eight. If masking fails, the previous
behaviour (all icon sizes as representations) is kept.
---
